old me to get down on the ground  and I was ultimately arrested for felony  vandalism and when I went to court the  case was not filed and I was very happy  but I'm currently out on bail for an  assault charge and I got out of prison  on my last case for aggravated assault  which is the exact same charges I'm on  bail for now but when I got arrested for  graffiti you cannot get arrested while  you're out on bail which I did so I  bailed out on that one before my other  bail cuff any kid find out but when I  went to court they dropped it well I got  a letter in the mail yesterday they just  filed it so not only they just filed the  graffiti charge that I thought was drops  this incident with the black eyes I got  another assault case and so now I'm on  bail for assault case felony vandalism  got an assault case pending all three of  these pending and I still do graffiti  every day so let's say I'm a business  owner I rent a space somewhere and I am  proud of my new business I mean yes we  clean it up and make it perfect and  that's my new place of business and then  one day I show up for work and there's  graffiti all over the building  how do you justify that it depends I  didn't I didn't approve it I didn't want  absolutely and so um every graffiti  writer has certain things that they're  willing to respect me personally I  respect people's personal property I  would never write on somebody's vehicle  or their home now  you mentioned a business it depends on  where that business is located if you  are in downtown LA or in downtown Skid  Row your shits fair game and the reason  being is because it's such a bad  neighborhood that this artwork  whether it's gang writing traditional  graffiti propaganda  huit pasting road signs there's gonna be  some sort of graffiti on your building  whether I do it or somebody else does it  but if you have a new building in a nice  area I would never touch that building  and the reason being is because not only  am i a businessman and I have my own  business and my own studio  I wouldn't want somebody to do that to  my [ __ ] but the thing of it is  everybody's different so when I was  painting on a business very near here  the business owner came out and in the  commission of doing this he threatened  me with a gun and said what in the world  would possess you to stand here so  brazenly and disrespect me in my  business and I said I beg to differ  what's your name and he didn't want to  shake my hand but it caused him to pause  and so on I asked him what his name was  I said my name is Asher and I'm actually  your neighbor and I live right down the  street and I have a studio across the  street and your building was covered  with garbage and so I was covering it up  in a way that I thought looked better  but I didn't mean to offend you and you  don't own this building but I understand  that you own it and now that I'd met you  I won't continue to do this but since I  started you should at least allow me to  finish and he said absolutely not  because I have this gun doesn't mean  that I'm afraid to use it  but I don't like my neighbors whatsoever  so please do it next door so I just  changed my camera that I was recording  and I shifted it and I went and finished  it next door so I mean it kind of just  depends on a case-by-case basis and I  think and my view of things  it's okay but it's because it's already  there it's already going to happen but I  definitely would not want it on my home  or my business a school or a church you  know things of that nature but that's me  I'm in my 40s I'm an old-school guy but  new kids new people you have to give  respect in order to receive it and if  they're from a street if they're from a  gang and a crew that does this graffiti  and they're proud of being vandals then  that's what they want to do the point is  to vandalize [ __ ] you know it's because  they're seeking an identity and that's  what it is about is [ __ ] the system  stick it to the man we don't pay taxes  we steal our supplies we don't abide by  rules in this society because it's a  bunch of [ __ ] and lies and we're artists  and we're young and we're free and we're  [ __ ] wild and we can do whatever we  choose but let's just be honest that  self-destructive behavior is only gonna  get you so far and so I've been dealing  with this for a long time and people ask  me why do you keep doing this like you  have children you have grandchildren  you're successful you're celebrated why  haven't you started doing something else  why haven't you stuck and what do you  get out of this headaches headaches but  it's my passion and Who I am and I don't  believe that I'm gonna perish that I'm  gonna go to jail even though I'm a pink  petal when I'm state-raised and this is  who I am  I used to feel that this was negativity  but now I realize this is not only Who I  am but it brought me to this point  and so if I didn't go through those  negativity in those trials of prison  especially out as a young man I wouldn't  be where I am now but unfortunately for  me I'm still carrying a lot of that  misperception of masculinity so god  forbid somebody step on my shoes or bump  into me because I'm gonna assault you  immediately without thinking about it  and then immediately after doing so I'm  gonna realize oh [ __ ] you messed up and  so when I was young my dad used to  always ask me even though we didn't live  together he would always say what's the  matter with you what's the matter with  you you don't  think what's the matter with you and it  got to the point where I started  thinking there was something wrong with  me you know like maybe I do have a  mental problem because if I punch this  guy or if I paint on this guy's building  and I get arrested or I go to jail  that's not only not smart but that's  self-destructive so maybe he's right but  in reality it wasn't until I started  paying severe consequences like going to  jail like losing my freedom like being  alienated from my family that I started  to slowly think about things but now  fast forward 25 years later why am I  still doing it  I don't believe I'm doing anything wrong  I think society is the one with the  problem  and I think that when I had my first  solo art show in a gallery in downtown  Los Angeles this year and I make an  extensive amount of money and then I  start traveling the world now  everybody's gonna say oh look this is my  nephew this is my brother oh look how  proud I am of my family member he's so  successful and only because a monetary  value or because I'm doing it in a  gallery so if I'm a successful tattooer  instead of painting the street or if I'm  instead of doing canvases so I choose my  canvas and I choose my art and where I  choose to put it but you're only  celebrated in certain ways and I think  that is uh not only ridiculous but I'm  willing to deal with the consequences  because authenticity cannot be faked or  duplicated and real will always rise to  the top so some people aren't the best  hustlers some people can't sell their  art some people have the best art  ability but don't have the hustle or the  knowledge of finances my thing is I have  no [ __ ] interest in those things I'm  a minimalist and I love being out here  and the fact that I'm not doing life in  prison the fact that I can walk outside  my studio on Skid Row and for the price  of a dollar can of spray paint paint  anywhere in Los Angeles knowing it'll  reach to the far ends of the world via  the internet I'm the happiest guy on  earth I might not have a dollar to my  name at some point I might be facing  over a decade in prison single all these  things against me but in reality I'm the  happiest that I've ever been because I'm  living my dream and I don't care what  anybody says I'm a part of history and  not only am I in the history books I'm  in the concrete in downtown Los Angeles  that [ __ ] is never going anywhere I'm in  the history books I'm on the rooftop of  this building in front of the street  downtown everywhere oh gee a sure Lok's  downtown Skid Row Los Angeles California  watch out for me  all right Asher thank you very much  thank you  you
 

